WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.021 --> 00:00:01.389
Wolf, it is still unclear if it

00:00:01.957 --> 00:00:03.124
would have enough votes to

00:00:03.391 --> 00:00:03.491
pass.

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:04.459
&gt;&gt; Manu, thank you very much.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.261
Manu Raju, up on capitol hill.

00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:07.362
Let's stay on capitol hill.

00:00:08.096 --> 00:00:09.264
Joining us now, congressman

00:00:09.531 --> 00:00:09.965
Adam Schiff.

00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:11.132
He's the Democrat of

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:11.600
California.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.500
Thank you so much for joining

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:12.834
us.

00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:15.103
We have a lot to discuss, but

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.238
first, what does it say to you

00:00:16.504 --> 00:00:17.472
that Republicans are now

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:18.406
gearing up for another attempt

00:00:19.074 --> 00:00:20.642
to censor you, after this

00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:21.343
latest effort today fail?

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.580
&gt;&gt; Well look.

00:00:25.981 --> 00:00:27.515
I'm flattered that they view me

00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:28.617
as such a threat to them.

00:00:29.251 --> 00:00:30.585
That they view me as effective

00:00:30.852 --> 00:00:32.254
at holding Donald Trump

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.555
accountable, and this is the

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:34.589
way they want to lash out.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.491
But it's not going to deter me.

00:00:36.758 --> 00:00:38.326
They can introduce all the

00:00:38.593 --> 00:00:39.361
resolutions they want, it could

00:00:39.628 --> 00:00:41.496
be 16 million or 160 million.

00:00:41.997 --> 00:00:43.531
I'm not going to stop defending

00:00:43.999 --> 00:00:44.032
our democracy.

00:00:44.299 --> 00:00:46.501
But, for the speaker Mccarthy

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.403
to bring this stuff to the

00:00:49.271 --> 00:00:50.005
floor is an embarrassment.

00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:51.573
And it's also an abuse of the

00:00:52.007 --> 00:00:52.440
house resources.

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:54.542
It would be laughable if you

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:56.378
had George Santos today saying

00:00:56.645 --> 00:00:57.412
we have to pass this to restore

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:58.680
integrity to the house.

00:00:58.947 --> 00:00:59.614
This stuff would be laughable

00:01:00.015 --> 00:01:02.250
if it wasn't the house of

00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:02.784
representatives.

00:01:03.351 --> 00:01:04.486
But it's clear the lunatics

00:01:04.753 --> 00:01:06.421
have taken over the asylum, and

00:01:07.222 --> 00:01:08.523
I want to try to distract from

00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:10.558
trump's legal woes, they want

00:01:10.825 --> 00:01:12.394
to gratify his Maga base by

00:01:12.661 --> 00:01:15.330
going after some of debt they

00:01:15.597 --> 00:01:16.298
considerate his chief

00:01:16.564 --> 00:01:16.765
antagonist.

00:01:17.032 --> 00:01:18.466
&gt;&gt; I know you have defended

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.201
your previous comments

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:22.404
defending collusion between

00:01:22.671 --> 00:01:23.405
trump and Russia --

00:01:23.672 --> 00:01:25.540
have you learned any lessons,

00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:27.442
congressman, on how to talk

00:01:27.709 --> 00:01:28.076
about his legal peril?

00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:34.049
&gt;&gt; Well, wolf, let's face it.

00:01:34.149 --> 00:01:35.684
Trump's campaign chairman Paul

00:01:36.051 --> 00:01:37.686
manafort, as you know, was

00:01:38.053 --> 00:01:38.820
giving internal campaign

00:01:39.087 --> 00:01:40.055
polling data and their

00:01:40.188 --> 00:01:41.690
battleground strategy for key

00:01:42.057 --> 00:01:43.625
states to an agent of Russian

00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:44.125
intelligence.

00:01:44.592 --> 00:01:45.593
Something that most Americans

00:01:46.061 --> 00:01:46.127
call collusion.

00:01:46.728 --> 00:01:48.863
So, my statements are accurate.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.666
I stand by them as I think the

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:52.434
American people do, but look.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.069
They are going to go after me

00:01:54.069 --> 00:01:54.336
no matter what.

00:01:54.636 --> 00:01:56.638
And I am just going to keep on

00:01:56.905 --> 00:01:58.073
defending the truth, and I'm

00:01:58.073 --> 00:01:59.641
going to keep on defending our

00:02:00.075 --> 00:02:00.709
democracy.

00:02:00.709 --> 00:02:02.077
The only lesson I take away

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.645
from this recent attack is if

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:04.946
you do your job and you stand

00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:06.681
up to the Maga world, you have

00:02:06.948 --> 00:02:08.083
to be prepared to take all of

00:02:08.249 --> 00:02:08.850
the income.

00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:09.684
I am prepared to do.

00:02:10.085 --> 00:02:12.087
So &gt;&gt; What concerns do you have

00:02:12.253 --> 00:02:14.689
about these calls by some house

00:02:14.956 --> 00:02:16.091
Republicans to subpoena the

00:02:16.191 --> 00:02:17.759
special counsel jack Smith, and

00:02:18.093 --> 00:02:18.994
to try to defund his entire

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:19.394
office?

00:02:19.661 --> 00:02:24.332
&gt;&gt; I think this is another

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:25.567
reason why they're going after

00:02:26.101 --> 00:02:26.334
me.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:27.669
I serve now as a senior member

00:02:28.103 --> 00:02:28.770
of the judiciary committee.

00:02:29.437 --> 00:02:30.638
Kevin Mccarthy may rue the day

00:02:30.905 --> 00:02:32.374
that he took me off until now,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.641
because I am in a position to

00:02:34.342 --> 00:02:35.477
push back against Jim Jordan

00:02:35.744 --> 00:02:36.678
and the Republicans on the

00:02:37.412 --> 00:02:38.113
committee effort to interfere

00:02:38.179 --> 00:02:39.347
in the prosecution of Donald

00:02:39.614 --> 00:02:39.714
Trump.

00:02:40.115 --> 00:02:43.585
As I said last week, Donald

00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:45.653
Trump has --

00:02:46.588 --> 00:02:47.022
criminal defense lawyers.

00:02:47.589 --> 00:02:48.823
That's not the job of members

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.125
of congress to be on his

00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:50.725
defense team.

00:02:50.992 --> 00:02:52.127
But this is what they are

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.528
trying to do and I'm going to

00:02:53.795 --> 00:02:54.696
resist those efforts in every

00:02:54.963 --> 00:02:55.730
way I can.

00:02:56.131 --> 00:02:58.666
It's absurd to me that you have

00:02:58.933 --> 00:03:00.135
so many Republicans attacking

00:03:00.235 --> 00:03:00.902
the justice department.

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:02.737
They were doing it before they

00:03:03.004 --> 00:03:04.606
even read the indictment, now

00:03:04.873 --> 00:03:06.141
presidential candidates are

00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:07.575
saying that they would pardon

00:03:08.143 --> 00:03:08.176
him.

00:03:08.176 --> 00:03:09.644
Clearly, in their view, it

00:03:10.145 --> 00:03:10.945
doesn't matter how many times

00:03:11.212 --> 00:03:12.647
he violates the law, doesn't

00:03:12.914 --> 00:03:14.616
matter how serious his

00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:15.784
transgressions, they will stand

00:03:16.151 --> 00:03:17.685
by him, because they think

00:03:18.153 --> 00:03:19.521
that's what the Republican base

00:03:19.788 --> 00:03:20.221
is at this moment.

00:03:20.488 --> 00:03:22.590
And they are willing to

00:03:22.857 --> 00:03:24.826
essentially ignore their oath

00:03:25.093 --> 00:03:26.161
